@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g3-operator.l4: section 18 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems
-- Law 5785-2025: the duties of an operator, the person who regularly engages others to work on cooling systems.
-- Written by ENCODER G3.  Imports only prelude, daydate and domain (no period is counted in section 18, so the time module is not needed).
--
-- What this module decides:
--   s.18(a)  an operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system unless that person holds a licence of the kind
--            appropriate to the system (SHANT).  The Third Schedule prices the breach in two items, (5) no licence at all and (6) no
--            licence of the appropriate kind; `Listed violation` carries which.
--   s.18(b)  an operator shall make sure that a licensee he engages works to the Standard of s.13 (MUST; a duty of conduct, fork S18-B).
--   s.18(c)  who an operator is.
--
-- Standard names taken from other groups (PLAN section (c)): `licence kinds in force on the day` (IP1, of the person engaged, on the day of
-- the engagement), the licence kinds that fit the system (IP3, G1's `licence kinds that cover a cooling system`, here
-- `licence kinds that cover the system`), `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` (IP2) and `the act is work on a cooling
-- system` (IP4).  Whether the operator "regularly" engages, and whether the measures taken were enough, are judgements: inputs.
--
-- Fork COM does not arise here: s.18 is about engaging a person in work on a cooling system, which is what s.63(a) fixes commencement for.
--
-- Forks and what the sources do not answer are in FRAGMENT-G3.md; the fork numbers in comments are its.

§ `Chapter 3 (continued): duties of an operator, section 18`

-- src:152 | {{ח:סעיף|18|חובות מפעיל}}

§§ `Nouns of section 18`

-- The acts that section 18 speaks of, named by what is done.
@ref s.18 (src:153-155)
DECLARE `Act under section 18 of the Law` IS ONE OF
    `engage a person in work on a cooling system`
    `take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard`

-- What a witness could say about a person who engages others: the two limbs of s.18(c) as facts.
@ref s.18(c) (src:155)
DECLARE `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` HAS
    `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the person regularly engages another person to perform work on cooling systems, whether or not the person holds a licence
    `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person is an owner or manager of a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public

-- The measures an operator took under (b).  The text names instructions, briefings, procedures and sample checks "inter alia": they
-- are examples, not conditions, so the record carries one judgement and no list of them.
@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
DECLARE `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` HAS
    `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the measures the operator took (instructions, briefings, procedures, sample checks or others) were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard of section 13

§§ `18(a). An operator shall not engage a person who lacks the appropriate licence`

-- src:153 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} מפעיל לא יפעיל אדם בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר, אלא אם כן יש בידי אותו אדם רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת.

-- "A licence of the kind appropriate to perform work on that system": one of the kinds in force is among the kinds that cover the system
-- (IP3 gives the second list, IP1 the first).  This is the positive answer to "may the operator engage the person?".
@ref s.18(a) (src:153)
@export Decides whether an operator may engage a person in work on a cooling system, that is, whether the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system (section 18(a))
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds that cover a system of the capacity of the cooling system (grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any), from the licensing group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    any (GIVEN kind YIELD elem kind `licence kinds that cover the system`) `licence kinds in force on the day`

-- The section binds an operator (18(c)), for an engagement in work on a cooling system, once the Law has commenced for that work.
@ref s.18(a) (src:153)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(a) — section 18(a) applies to the engagement` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
        `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` facts
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND `the act is work on a cooling system`

@ref s.18(a) (src:153)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
        `s.18(a) — section 18(a) applies to the engagement` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system`

-- The Third Schedule splits the breach into item (5), "no licence at all", and item (6), "not of the appropriate kind".  Taken (fork S18-H):
-- a person "has" a licence when it is in force, so no kind in force is item (5) and some kind in force, none of them appropriate, is item (6).
-- src:718 and src:721 are items (5) and (6).
-- src:718 | {{ח:תת|(5)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון כלל, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
-- src:721 | {{ח:תת|(6)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
@ref s.18(a) (src:153); Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (src:718-721)
@export Returns the Third Schedule violation an operator committed by engaging a person without a licence (item 5) or without a licence of the appropriate kind (item 6), or nothing
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` @desc Whether the person regularly engages others in work on cooling systems and whether the person owns or manages a business offering such work to the public
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system, an act of a kind the First Schedule lists (decided by the licensing group)
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds that cover a system of the capacity of the cooling system (grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any), from the licensing group
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    IF   `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system`
    THEN (IF   null `licence kinds in force on the day`
          THEN JUST `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
          ELSE JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Alternative S18-H: a licence the person holds but that is not in force (expired, revoked, suspended) is still a licence "in his hand",
-- so item (5) needs that the person holds no licence of any kind, in force or not.
@ref s.18(a) (src:153); Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (src:718-721)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `licence kinds held, in force or not` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), a licence held but not in force being a licence held` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds held, in force or not` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    IF   `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system`
    THEN (IF   null `licence kinds held, in force or not`
          THEN JUST `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
          ELSE JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Alternative S18-D: s.18(c) defines "operator" "in this section" only, and Third Schedule items (5) and (6) use the word.  If the definition did not reach
-- them, the items would use an undefined word and no answer could be given: a named refusal.
@ref s.18(c) (src:155); Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (src:718-721)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s.18(c) — the word operator in Third Schedule items (5) and (6) is defined only for section 18, so the items cannot be applied` MEANS
    REFUSE "s.18(c): the word operator is defined only for section 18, so Third Schedule items (5) and (6), which use it, cannot be applied to anyone"

@ref s.18(c) (src:155); Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (src:718-721)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), the word operator of the Third Schedule being undefined` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    `s.18(c) — the word operator in Third Schedule items (5) and (6) is defined only for section 18, so the items cannot be applied`

-- The record Chapter 6 takes (IP9): the violator is the operator, a person who may be an individual or a corporation.
@ref s.18(a) (src:153); Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (src:718-721)
@export Returns the violation record for Chapter 6 when an operator engaged a person without the appropriate licence, or nothing
GIVEN operator IS A Person @desc The operator, as a person
      `reference for the act` IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies the act; two violations with the same reference are one act
      `the day of the engagement` IS A DATE @desc The day the operator engaged the person
      facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` @desc Whether the person regularly engages others in work on cooling systems and whether the person owns or manages a business offering such work to the public
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system, an act of a kind the First Schedule lists (decided by the licensing group)
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds that cover a system of the capacity of the cooling system (grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any), from the licensing group
GIVETH A MAYBE Violation
`s.18(a) — the violation committed under section 18(a)` operator `reference for the act` `the day of the engagement` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST listed THEN JUST (Violation WITH
        `the violator` IS operator
        `the listed violation` IS listed
        `reference for the act` IS `reference for the act`
        `date of the act` IS `the day of the engagement`)

-- "Shall not engage ... unless": a prohibition standing for as long as the person is an operator, so no WITHIN.  The guard says what makes
-- the engagement a prohibited one: the person engaged lacks a licence of the appropriate kind.
@ref s.18(a) (src:153)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `licence kinds that cover the system` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 18 of the Law`
`s.18(a) — the operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system without a licence of the appropriate kind` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system` MEANS
    IF   `s.18(a) — section 18(a) applies to the engagement` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    THEN PARTY `the operator`
         SHANT `engage a person in work on a cooling system`
               PROVIDED NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `licence kinds in force on the day` `licence kinds that cover the system`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the operator` BECAUSE "s.18(a): the operator engaged a person in work on a cooling system who held no licence of the kind appropriate to the system"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `18(b). An operator shall make sure that the licensees he engages work to the Standard`

-- src:154 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} מפעיל יוודא כי בעל רישיון שהוא מפעיל יבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר כמפורט {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|בתוספת הראשונה}} בהתאם לתקן כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 13|בסעיף 13}}, בין השאר באמצעות הנחיות, תדריכים או נהלים וביצוע בדיקות מדגמיות.

-- "Shall make sure that a licensee he engages performs the work ... in accordance with the Standard of s.13, inter alia by instructions,
-- briefings or procedures and sample checks."  Sample checks cannot guarantee a result, which is the ground of the reading taken (fork S18-B):
-- the duty is one of conduct, met by measures sufficient to make sure; sufficiency is a judgement, an input.
-- The duty needs a licensee who is engaged: an operator engaging nobody, or only the unlicensed, has nothing under (b) (s.18(a) catches those).
@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` MEANS
        `s.18(a) — section 18(a) applies to the engagement` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND NOT (null `licence kinds in force on the day`)

@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
@export Decides whether an operator took the measures that section 18(b) requires to make sure a licensee works to the Standard
GIVEN measures IS A `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` @desc The measures the operator took, and the judgement whether they were sufficient to make sure the licensee would work to the Standard
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(b) — the operator took the section 18(b) steps` measures MEANS
    measures's `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard`

@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      measures IS A `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` measures MEANS
        `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND NOT `s.18(b) — the operator took the section 18(b) steps` measures

-- Alternative S18-B: a duty of result, breached whenever a licensee the operator engaged did not work to the Standard of section 13.
-- The finding that the work conformed is the licensee's own finding under section 13, an input here.
@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the licensee's work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b), the duty being one of result` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the licensee's work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994` MEANS
        `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND NOT `the licensee's work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: a MUST with no time stated (so no WITHIN).  The act that discharges it is taking steps that suffice;
-- the guard carries the judgement.  Because no deadline is stated, a trace can show the duty discharged or standing but not breached;
-- the breach is the decision `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)`.
@ref s.18(b) (src:154)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      measures IS A `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 18 of the Law`
`s.18(b) — the operator must make sure that the licensee works to the Standard` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` measures MEANS
    IF   `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` facts `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    THEN PARTY `the operator`
         MUST `take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard`
              PROVIDED `s.18(b) — the operator took the section 18(b) steps` measures
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `18(c). Who is an operator`

-- src:155 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} בסעיף זה, ”מפעיל“ – מי שמפעיל, דרך קבע, אדם אחר בביצוע עבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר, בין שהמפעיל הוא בעל רישיון ובין שאינו בעל רישיון, ובכלל זה מי שהוא בעלים או מנהל של עסק המציע לציבור ביצוע עבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר.

-- "One who regularly engages another person in work on cooling systems, whether the operator holds a licence or not, and including one who
-- owns or manages a business that offers such work to the public."  Taken (fork S18-C): the business limb is a limb of its own, so the owner
-- or manager of such a business is an operator by that status, as well as by regular engagement.  The licence of the operator is irrelevant.
@ref s.18(c) (src:155)
@export Decides whether a person is an operator under section 18(c): one who regularly engages another person in work on cooling systems, or who owns or manages a business offering such work to the public
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` @desc Whether the person regularly engages others in work on cooling systems and whether the person owns or manages a business offering such work to the public
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(c) — the person is an operator` facts MEANS
        facts's `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems`
    OR  facts's `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public`

-- Alternative S18-C: "including" only illustrates the main limb, so the owner or manager is an operator only if he regularly engages another person.
@ref s.18(c) (src:155)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.18(c) — the person is an operator, the business limb being only an illustration` facts MEANS
    facts's `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems`
